  "body": "Ports three engagement pins from PR #3439 onto main's Pass start law\n(`crates/motion/src/machining2d/level_rings.rs` and `level_order.rs`).\nThe change is test-only. It changes no product code.\n\n## What is ported\n\n- `outside_on_a_figure_eight_band_never_slots`: Outside on a synthetic\n  figure-eight band cuts no wider than 1.5 stepovers over any 3 tool\n  radii of floor feed. Main pins this law only in the ignored heavy app\n  test `fig8_outside_offset_cuts_no_move_at_full_width`. This pin gives\n  default-suite coverage.\n- `inside_on_the_band_clears_the_whole_band`: Inside on the round-part\n  band leaves less than 0.5 mm2 of stock off the part wall. It checks\n  both climb directions.\n- `auto_on_the_band_slots_so_the_measure_sees_a_slot`: Auto (core first)\n  on the same band slots. This pin is the positive control for the width\n  measure.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Test | Result | Time |\n|---|---|---|\n| outside_on_a_figure_eight_band_never_slots | pass | 0.94 s |\n| inside_on_the_band_clears_the_whole_band | pass | 2.08 s |\n| auto_on_the_band_slots_so_the_measure_sees_a_slot | pass | 0.55 s |\n\nEach test ran alone in debug with `-j 3`:\n`cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test pass_start_engagement -- --exact <name>`.\n\n## Not ported\n\n- `outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock` fails on main.\n  The later entries cut 332.88 mm2 of uncut stock. Main's law does not\n  lead a re-entry from cleared stock.\n- `outside_on_a_split_band_never_slots` repeats main. The test\n  `outside_band_split_by_the_part_cuts_no_move_at_full_width` already\n  pins the same Outside split-band law.\n- `pass_start::tests::a_start_on_a_wall_is_named_and_a_start_in_air_is_not`\n  does not apply. It calls `start_wall_note`, which main replaced with\n  `StartSide::wall_first_note`. Its assertions name one string that main\n  splits into two strings.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe figure-eight STEP app test stays in its heavy lane. This PR does not\nchange it and does not run it.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #3316\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
